## Alternative Approach with Interface

If you want even more flexibility, you could create an interface:

```csharp
public interface IDepthLevel
{
    int Level { get; set; }
}

public interface IGraphTree<T> : IDepthLevel where T : IEntity
{
    List<T> TreeNodes { get; set; }
}

public class GenericGraphTree<T> : T, IGraphTree<T> where T : IEntity, new()
{
    public int Level { get; set; }
    public List<T> TreeNodes { get; set; } = [];
}
```

This approach allows you to use the same pattern with any entity type that implements `IEntity`, making your code much more reusable and maintainable.

