Creating an equivalent of an Erlang/OTP runtime in Rust using Tokio, Wasmer, and Cap'n Proto over QUIC is a complex task that involves several components. Below is a high-level overview and a simplified example to get you started. This example will cover the basic structure and some key components, but a full implementation would require more detailed work.

